  "label": "prop:lusztig-vs-hermitian-bar",
  "kind": "proposition",
  "title": "Lusztig bar ($q \\mapsto q^{-1}$) vs Hermitian-$\\ast$ ($q \\mapsto \\overline{q}^{-1}$) on the complex Hecke algebra: the two anti-involutions coincide on the parameter iff $q \\in \\mathbb{R}$. On the unit circle $|q| = 1$, Lusztig coincides with complex conjugation ($\\overline{q} = q^{-1}$) while Hermitian becomes the identity on $q$; on general $|q| > 1$ with $\\mathrm{Im}(q) \\neq 0$ the three involutions (Lusztig, Hermitian, complex conjugation) are pairwise distinct. The split is the categorical home for any future $\\mathrm{Im}(q_0)$ contribution.",
